I assume it's mostly about the right attitude.  Like Dave put it 
once:  Play as if it were your life on stage there.  Would *you* 
really quaff a potion you have no idea what it might do while in 
a hostile dungeon?  Would *you* really allow those orcs to surround 
you while you fight their leader toe-to-toe?  Would *you* really 
hesitate to hit a dangerous monster from far away with a wand of 
magic missile 'because I might need it sometimes later'?  (I don't 
want to indicate that you play this way, I just know I did.) 

> I have just found a second =oC. Is there any benefit in having two, or
> should I dump one?

Actually, at the current stage there's little benefit in having 
one.  However, you can stash them away; first they'll be useful 
much later, second, you might polymorph them into hopefully more 
useful rings (but that's also much later).  For now, care about 
food (spellcasting is very foodconsuming), speed, AC and your 
pet.  

